        "payload": "tree 2abf11d0e32703e7b4709f2527c05ead97fc3345\nparent 5b4efb74c751c33123a39821bf8e4f0ff12afe6d\nauthor rabble <evan@protest.net> 1779243330 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779243330 +1200\n\nfeat: admin restore endpoint for previously banned usernames (#52)\n\nAdds POST /api/admin/username/restore for the moderation service's ban-reversal flow:\nwhen a creator's ban is lifted, restore re-binds their previously-revoked or burned\n<name>.divine.video URL to the original pubkey.\n\nBehavior:\n- 200: flips status -> active, recyclable=1, revoked_at=NULL, sets pubkey, resets\n  claimed_at to now, appends a timestamped audit line to admin_notes, and re-syncs\n  the row to Fastly KV via waitUntil.\n- 404 when the row does not exist.\n- 409 when the row is currently active (response includes current_pubkey so the\n  caller can decide whether to revoke first); silently overwriting active claims\n  is forbidden.\n- Releases any other active name held by the target pubkey before flipping (mirrors\n  assignUsername; required by the partial unique index on (pubkey, status='active')).\n- Reuses validateUsername / validateAndNormalizePubkey for input validation.\n\nTests cover restore-from-burned, restore-from-revoked, 404, 409-over-active, invalid\npubkey, missing fields, and a regression that revoke{burn:true} preserves pubkey so\nGET /usernames/search?q=<pubkey>&status=burned still discovers the row.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
